# 高频词汇 List07
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 高频词汇List07核心词汇

{{participate}}{/pɑːˈtɪsɪpeɪt/}{参加；参与}{All students are encouraged to participate in the discussion.}}
{{perceive}}{/pəˈsiːv/}{感知；认为}{The policy was perceived as unfair by many citizens.}}
{{perform}}{/pəˈfɔːm/}{执行；表演}{The company performed well despite the economic downturn.}}
{{perspective}}{/pəˈspektɪv/}{观点；视角}{The book offers a fresh perspective on modern history.}}
{{phenomenon}}{/fɪˈnɒmɪnən/}{现象；非凡的人或事}{Climate change is a global phenomenon with local impacts.}}
{{policy}}{/ˈpɒləsi/}{政策；方针}{The new policy aims to reduce traffic congestion.}}
{{positive}}{/ˈpɒzətɪv/}{积极的；肯定的}{A positive mindset can improve your overall well-being.}}
{{potential}}{/pəˈtenʃl/}{潜力；潜在的}{The technology has enormous potential for growth.}}
{{predict}}{/prɪˈdɪkt/}{预测；预言}{It is hard to predict how the market will react.}}
{{preserve}}{/prɪˈzɜːv/}{保护；保存}{Efforts to preserve the rainforest have intensified.}}
{{previous}}{/ˈpriːviəs/}{以前的；先前的}{Her previous experience made her ideal for the role.}}
{{primary}}{/ˈpraɪməri/}{主要的；初级的}{The primary concern is public safety.}}
{{principle}}{/ˈprɪnsəpl/}{原则；原理}{The design is based on the principle of sustainability.}}
{{priority}}{/praɪˈɒrəti/}{优先事项；重点}{Improving education is the government's top priority.}}
{{proceed}}{/prəˈsiːd/}{继续；进行}{After the interruption, the meeting proceeded normally.}}
{{process}}{/ˈprəʊses/}{过程；处理}{The hiring process takes approximately four weeks.}}
{{produce}}{/prəˈdjuːs/}{生产；产生}{The region produces high-quality agricultural products.}}
{{professional}}{/prəˈfeʃənl/}{专业的；职业人员}{She has over 20 years of professional experience.}}
{{profit}}{/ˈprɒfɪt/}{利润；利益}{The company reported a significant increase in profit.}}
{{profound}}{/prəˈfaʊnd/}{深刻的；深远的}{The book had a profound impact on my thinking.}}
{{progress}}{/ˈprəʊɡres/}{进步；进展}{Good progress has been made toward the goal.}}
{{promote}}{/prəˈməʊt/}{促进；推广}{The program promotes healthy eating habits among children.}}
{{property}}{/ˈprɒpəti/}{财产；性质}{The property market has been volatile in recent years.}}
{{propose}}{/prəˈpəʊz/}{提议；建议}{The committee proposed a new framework for regulation.}}
{{prospect}}{/ˈprɒspekt/}{前景；展望}{The prospects for economic recovery look promising.}}
{{protest}}{/prəˈtest/}{抗议；反对}{Citizens held a peaceful protest outside the parliament.}}
{{provide}}{/prəˈvaɪd/}{提供；供给}{The university provides scholarships for outstanding students.}}
{{pursue}}{/pəˈsjuː/}{追求；追赶}{She decided to pursue a master's degree abroad.}}
{{qualify}}{/ˈkwɒlɪfaɪ/}{使合格；取得资格}{The team qualified for the national championship.}}
{{range}}{/reɪndʒ/}{范围；山脉}{The course covers a wide range of topics.}}
